event_uuid":"38503094-dbc6-481a-b706-38a21c676d24","position":{"commit_sha":"3ac7d94684aefef5b3bad5695f64be945e5b8255","position":"1788239410465245001-38503094-dbc6-481a-b706-38a21c676d24"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3e6da45675b7e82159b01fc5387ab38447c72fe5cbabeedc08d5f9ede8354987","event_uuid":"d5eaed8f-6de9-4a02-b444-9efd8e33875a","position":{"commit_sha":"90a249bf477ac4282dad4b0ecd341cf9f63ce50b","position":"1788239418005449001-d5eaed8f-6de9-4a02-b444-9efd8e33875a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e3f5d761c7169d4c7a23e108830dd1a21ccb3ea8a8cd5b4fb3cfc46545b37f2e","event_uuid":"699e14a4-1339-491b-a115-2dcffa73889b","position":{"commit_sha":"afc6e88ecca50011ac56fff3c1574decbfb497a0","position":"1788239422391222001-699e14a4-1339-491b-a115-2dcffa73889b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"20d16b05965aae4baf822ee0fb9e9423c93a50ee2f78b6bc69763c4c61f9e783","event_uuid":"81acdabf-b960-4d2c-94be-bd18c6891f37","position":{"commit_sha":"03bb7315bce8265f46e97617cac75a0699df7212","position":"1788239470792728001-81acdabf-b960-4d2c-94be-bd18c6891f37"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA confirmation and disposition\n\nStep 0: duplicate sweep found prior closed duplicate `linty-sunshiny-gull` / `94a3-1323-3497-4f59`, whose fix is already merged on current `origin/main`. Report floor from this ticket's `created_at` is `05be3a4dc6e48d982006cc5532904cd17add41eb`; worktree HEAD is current `origin/main` (`1299d9deb6da82708bf694e19572ef8579664f34`).\n\nConfirmed RCA on current `origin/main`: plan material is a single composite hash over basis keys from `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py` (`ticket_id`, normalized `description`, `file_impact`, `children`, plus conditional `file_impact_scope`) and `pass1.material_fingerprint()` delegates to that basis. Checkbox state is normalized out by `normalize_checkbox_state`, so a tick-only AC edit is attestation-safe; local reproduction printed equal hashes for unticked vs ticked descriptions. The pre-fix failure was diagnostic: stale-material reasons used a fixed/fictional list (`description/AC/file_impact/children`) rather than signed per-component material.\n\nDefect origin: commit `66f0220d747f6eda5cd15986d4c8659bbf88096a` (epic `dark-acme-lumen`, `4702-a55c-7aeb-445a`) introduced kind-keyed attestations and `compute_validity`, including the fixed stale-material wording. The plan itself described the material as `description/AC/file_impact/children`, so this is attributed as `plan_defect` caused by `dark-acme-lumen`.\n\nFix/verification: existing merged Gerrit change 1434 (`4b5a7bcd4adf744d96ba98fcd953afa3c37d780e`, ticket `94a3-1323-3497-4f59`) adds additive `material-part:` manifest lines, component-wise explanation, and the refusal-surface parity updates. RED oracle on pre-fix parent `34998a2ca835...` failed because the stale completion-material reason did not contain `file_impact`; current targeted suite passes: `pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py -q` => 113 passed. Sandboxed mutation restoring the old completion-verifier stale-material message returned RED (12 failures in the material-diff test file). Full `pytest tests/unit tests/integration -q` reached one unrelated environment failure: `tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py::test_delete_permission_probe` cannot create a Jira item because ACLI is not authenticated.\n\nStep 7 sweep: `git grep` over `src/rebar` finds no remaining `description/AC/file_impact/children` runtime literal. `compute_validity` stale-material uses `explain_material_change`; `claim_gate_check` forwards validity reasons and names both unsigned remedies; `generation.py` and `resign.py` name own/dependency material drift; `completion_child_gate.py` forwards the child signature reason; `_cli/_llm_commands.py` special-cases `plan_review_sign_aborted` store-read-failure. `stale-code`/`stale-head` and cryptographic op-cert/signing errors already name their differing files/SHAs/keys and were correctly left alone.\n","timestamp":1788239359917241001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Final debug report\n\nProblem: `gastric-handy-angelfish` duplicated the already-landed 94a3 diagnostic bug: stale attestation messages failed to name what changed.\n\nRoot cause/proof: current `origin/main` confirms the material basis is componentized in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py` and `pass1.material_fingerprint()` delegates to it; checkbox state normalization makes tick-only AC edits safe (local reproduction: unticked and ticked descriptions hash equal). The prior fixed-list message came from commit `66f0220d747f6eda5cd15986d4c8659bbf88096a` under `dark-acme-lumen` (`4702-...`), so the closed bug records explicit `caused_by=dark-acme-lumen`.\n\nRED→GREEN: a held-out pre-fix oracle on parent `34998a2ca835...` failed because the stale completion-material reason did not contain `file_impact`. On current main, `pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py -q` passed (113 tests). Sandboxed mutation restoring the old reason made the material-diff suite RED (12 failures), proving test teeth.\n\nFix/land: Gerrit change 1434 (`4b5a7bcd4adf744d96ba98fcd953afa3c37d780e`) is MERGED with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. It adds signed additive `material-part:` lines, component diffs, and parity updates for claim/status/sign-review/generation/resign/child-completion/CLI surfaces. No gate outcome changed.\n\nStep 7/replication: runtime `src/rebar` contains no `description/AC/file_impact/children` literal; enumerated refusal surfaces either now forward/name the reason or were dispositioned as already-specific (`stale-code`, `stale-head`, cryptographic key/id mismatches). Original report no longer reproduces on current main. Full `pytest tests/unit tests/integration -q` was attempted; the only failure was unrelated environment auth (`test_delete_permission_probe`: ACLI not authenticated).\n\nDisposition: linked this ticket as `duplicates` of `linty-sunshiny-gull` / `94a3-1323-3497-4f59`, recorded explicit `caused_by=dark-acme-lumen`, and closed it as `duplicate` with a signed disposition attestation.","timestamp":1788239470792728001}],"completion_expectation":"disposition","created_at":1788216907674013001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f78e2b2d-665f-4a2b-a9f2-78d77373980d","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"94a3-1323-3497-4f59"},{"link_uuid":"699e14a4-1339-491b-a115-2dcffa73889b","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"4702-a55c-7aeb-445a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAttestation staleness errors currently say the plan changed in the fixed list \"description/AC/file_impact/children\". That is misleading: AC is not an independent material key, checkbox state is normalized out, and the message does not identify the component that actually changed. Operator approval: fix this broadly anywhere rebar reports an attestation refusal, including additive signed-manifest metadata, while preserving all gate outcomes.\n\n## Confirmed RCA\n\n`material_fingerprint()` hashes a single composite basis. Current `origin/main` keeps the basis single-sourced in `material_diff.material_basis`: `ticket_id`, normalized `description`, `file_impact`, `children`, and conditional `file_impact_scope`; `pass1.material_fingerprint()` hashes that basis. Checkbox state is removed by `normalize_checkbox_state()`, so ticking `- [ ]` to `- [x]` is attestation-safe. Because the composite hash is one-way and older manifests lack per-component values, stale-material readers could not name what changed and sometimes named the fictional `AC` component.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd signed per-component material fingerprints as deterministic additive `material-part: <name> <hash16> <size>` manifest lines. Parse them leniently and use them only for diagnostics. On stale-material, compare signed parts with live parts and render the changed component(s) plus compact sizes; legacy manifests fall back to child-pin add/remove diffs when possible, otherwise say the component cannot be named and advise re-review. Update every attestation-refusal surface that drops or rewrites the underlying reason so it forwards or reconstructs the same specific reason.\n\nInvariant: no gate outcome changes. Edits may only add manifest diagnostic lines or change `reason` text for already-failing branches. Do not change branch conditions, verdict names, thresholds, or valid/invalid decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`: per-component material hashing and explanation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py`: emit/parse additive `material-part:` lines.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py`: named stale-material reasons and timestamped stale-reopened reasons.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py`: actionable unsigned message and complete verdict docs.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py`: named own/dependency material drift.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`: named plan drift in sign-review recovery.\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py`: forward child closure signature reason.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`: sign-aborted rendering that names reason/remedy.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`: document checkbox-safe and named staleness reasons.\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py`: regression coverage.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the new material-diff unit tests first RED and then GREEN, then run the related existing suites: `tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py`, `tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py`, `tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py`, `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py`, plus `pytest tests/unit tests/integration` for the requested full gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `material_components(ctx)` exposes exactly the material basis keys, and changing one component changes only that component hash.\n- [ ] `build_manifest` emits sorted `material-part` lines; `manifest_material_parts()` round-trips them; manifests without lines parse to `{}`.\n- [ ] `compute_validity` stale-material reasons name changed components for description-only, file-impact-only, and children-only edits, never `description/AC/file_impact/children`.\n- [ ] Tick-only checkbox edits remain `verdict == \"certified\"`.\n- [ ] Legacy raw-description attestations over unchanged tickets remain certified.\n- [ ] Un-grandfatherable legacy attestations say the changed component cannot be named.\n- [ ] `stale-reopened` names signed and reopened timestamps.\n- [ ] `unsigned` names both `review-plan` and `sign-review` remedies.\n- [ ] `plan_review_sign_aborted` with `store-read-failure` renders that reason and does not advise `sign-review`.\n- [ ] Generation-time dependency material drift names changed dependency ticket ids.\n- [ ] Touched branches preserve the prior `(valid, verdict)` outcome.\n- [ ] Relevant unit and integration tests pass.\n- [ ] Documentation states plainly that ticking an AC checkbox is attestation-safe.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py","reason":"new: per-component material hashing and the changed-component explainer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"emit and parse additive material-part: lines"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"component-named stale-material reasons; timestamp-named stale-reopened"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"actionable unsigned message; corrected verdict vocabulary docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py","reason":"replace the fixed-list wording; name the changed dependency ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","reason":"replace the fixed-list staleness wording"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"forward the child-closure validity reason, not just the verdict"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"dedicated render branch for a sign-aborted failure naming its reason and remedy"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document that ticking a checkbox is attestation-safe and the new reasons"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py","reason":"new: per-verdict message tests, 330c pin, legacy regression, gate-invariance"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"38503094-dbc6-481a-b706-38a21c676d24","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[]